# iOS host

This folder is the Swift/UIKit host source for the Akari app. Rust owns the
shared interface; Swift starts Winit after UIKit has initialized.

On macOS with Xcode and the Rust iOS target installed:

```sh
cargo build --release --lib --target aarch64-apple-ios --no-default-features --features ios
```

Create an iOS App target in Xcode, add `AppDelegate.swift`, and set the target's
Objective-C Bridging Header to `ios/Akari-Bridging-Header.h`. Link
`target/aarch64-apple-ios/release/lib{{crate_name}}.a` under **Link Binary With
Libraries**. Add the UIKit, Metal, QuartzCore, and CoreGraphics system
frameworks. For simulator builds, build the matching Rust target and link its
static library instead.

This starter includes the native entry point and build instructions; an Xcode
project file and signing settings are created on the macOS app machine.
